  - Arm **A-NVTX** (eager with per-sublayer NVTX hooks) as a *separate* arm for attribution only —
    hooks change compiled graphs, so compiled arms are attributed from generated code, never hooks.
  - Exploratory hypothesis (labelled exploratory, directional only): fusion and concurrency give
    speedup beyond graphed compilation at 4410; no numeric ratio registered without derivation.
0.2 Add the **task-quality gate**: 8 fixed clips (public, e.g. MUSDB18-HQ test excerpts), SDR/SI-SDR
  of every arm's output vs the eager arm's output and vs reference stems; a common threshold
  (e.g. ΔSDR ≥ −0.1 dB vs eager) required of every arm compared on speed. Tolerance tiers remain
  for numerical equivalence; SDR is the application gate.
0.3 Runtime verification script for graph deployment: for C1/C3/H log cudagraph-trees graph count
  per pass, uncaptured ops, replay count, graph-launch count (from trace + `torch._inductor`
