## Phase 1 — Measurement session (agent, two pod sessions ≤ 3 h each)
1.1 **Arm matrix, unprofiled:** A, B, C1, C2, C3, D, E, F, G, H × {352800, 4410} (+ 22050 and
  88200 for A, C3, G, H only — the chunk sweep, four points). Protocol 5a. Validation at tiers +
  SDR gate. Planted-fault check first (registered prediction: FAIL both seeds, seed-invariant
  `max_abs_diff`).
1.2 **C1 vs C3 matched:** same session, interleaved repeats; plus C1 + attention-fix-only and
  C1 + DC-filter-fix-only. Output: the graph-break tax with each fix isolated, at matched clocks.
1.3 **Traces (node-level) for A, C3, G, H at both operating points.** Kernel table with
  classification (GEMM / SDPA / Inductor-fused / copy / FFT / other), NVTX sublayer ranges for
  A-NVTX only; for compiled arms, kernel→source-op mapping from `output_code` + Inductor
  provenance.
1.4 **Per-kernel ideal costs:** for every kernel row, FLOPs and minimum bytes from shapes;
  roofline ideal `max(FLOPs/P, bytes/BW)` with P = 209.5 TFLOPS (fp16, FP32-acc) or the fp32/TF32
  rate for kernels that run there (read dtype from the trace), BW = 1.79 TB/s HBM or L2 rate when the
  working set fits L2 (5090 L2 capacity from `nvidia-smi`/cudaGetDeviceProperties). Report both
  definitions where they differ.
1.5 **Attention backend microbench:** time-axis (801) and freq-axis (60) SDPA at model shapes,
  flash vs mem-efficient vs cuDNN vs math, fp16, on the 5090. Output: best backend per axis and
  the ratio to the backend the model actually uses (from the trace).
1.6 **Profiling perturbation:** for A, C3, G at 4410 and 8 s: wall unprofiled vs under graph-level
  tracing vs under node-level tracing. Report the ratios; if node-level inflates wall by >5% for
  any arm, all mechanism numbers from that trace carry the inflation factor as a caveat.
1.7 **Three timing views for multi-stream arms (F, G):** summed kernel durations, union of
  kernel intervals, and a dependency-critical-path estimate (from NVTX/stream structure; state
  the dependency model used). Never report "busy" without saying which.
1.8 Deliverables: `evidence/` (JSON/CSV/nsys), `SESSION_RESULT.md` in the fixed format from the
  scoping study (decision inputs, thresholds applied mechanically, predictions vs measurements,
  per-layer tables, what failed).

## Phase 2 — The Opportunity Ledger (agent, no GPU, 2 days)
For each candidate X below, compute at each operating point O ∈ {8 s, 4410} (and the sweep
where relevant):

```
Y(X, O) = T_attributable(X, O) × f_recoverable(X)      [ms]      Z = Y / T_wall(best arm, O)
```
with: `T_attributable` from Phase-1 traces (which kernels, which NVTX/provenance ranges);
`f_recoverable` from a stated mechanism (roofline ideal, backend ratio, boundary-cost model,
or 1.0 for "eliminate entirely"); confidence ∈ {A: measured directly; B: measured inputs +
simple model; C: model with untested assumption}; effort class ∈ {config, wrapper, kernel,
architecture}; prior work (who has done X on what); quality risk (none / numerical / task-level).
A ceiling is always an **upper bound**; state what would make the realized value lower.

Candidate X list (extend if the traces show something not listed):

| # | X | T_attributable from | f_recoverable model | Effort | Quality risk |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| X1 | Graph-break removal (C1→C3) | 1.2 matched | measured, not modelled | wrapper | none (validated) |
| X2 | Epilogue fusion into GEMMs (Inductor templates / hand) | Inductor elementwise kernels adjacent to GEMMs (bias/GELU/residual/norm) | 1 − (ideal fused epilogue bytes / current bytes); upper bound = their whole time | config→kernel | numerical |
| X3 | Attention backend selection per axis | SDPA kernels per axis | 1 − t_best/t_current (1.5) | config | numerical |
| X4 | Head-merge copy elimination | the 12 copy kernels (measured 0.89% at 8 s) | 1.0 | wrapper | none |
| X5 | Band-split + mask-estimator restructuring (pad-and-batch vs grouped vs current) | their kernels | H arm measured; grouped residual = padded FLOPs waste at roofline | wrapper/kernel | none |
| X6 | Elementwise/norm/RoPE/gating traffic (beyond X2) | all Inductor-fused pointwise/reduction kernels | 1 − (min bytes at BW / current time) | kernel | numerical |
| X7 | STFT / iSTFT | FFT + windowing kernels | 1 − (FFT roofline / current) | kernel | numerical |
| X8 | FP8 GEMMs (offline) | all GEMM kernels | 1 − (fp16 rate / fp8 rate) ≈ 0.5 on GB202 for FP32-acc | kernel/config | **task-level (SDR)** |
| X9 | fp16-accumulate GEMMs (GeForce full rate) | all GEMM kernels | ≤ 0.5 | kernel | **task-level** |
| X10 | Kernel-count reduction at 4410 (fusion) | N_kernels(best arm) × c_boundary(measured 0.4) − ideal compute | model: c_boundary × (N_current − N_floor), N_floor = kernels that cannot be fused without a megakernel | kernel | numerical |
| X11 | Concurrency at 4410 (independent bands/heads on streams inside graphs) | serialized sum vs critical path (1.7) | 1 − (critical path / serialized) | wrapper | none |
| X12 | Persistent megakernel at 4410 | wall(best arm) − critical-path compute − measured sync floor | upper bound only; realistic range from Hazy/Mirage (1.5–3× over graphs) | architecture | numerical |
| X13 | Mask-estimator MLP chain fusion (Tanh/GLU epilogues, 88% params/5% time) | its kernels | roofline | kernel | numerical |
| X14 | Cross-chunk batching for throughput (not latency) | whole pass | Amdahl over fixed costs; report separately as throughput | wrapper | none |

Ledger output `LEDGER.md`: one row per (X, O): Y ms, Z %, confidence, effort, prior work, quality
risk, "would be lower if …", and the evidence paths. Sorted by Z within each O. Plus a
**stacking note**: which X's overlap (X2/X6/X13 share kernels; X8/X9 are alternatives), so the
owner doesn't sum overlapping ceilings.

## Phase 3 — Owner review and deep dives (owner + agents)
3.1 Owner audits the ledger rows above the thresholds (15 minutes each: recompute Y from the
  cited CSV; check the attributable kernel set; check the f_recoverable assumption).
3.2 **Thresholds for "impressive" (owner may change before reading the ledger):**
  - Offline 8 s (deployed): Z ≥ 5% end-to-end with confidence A/B, or Z ≥ 10% with confidence C.
  - Streaming 4410 (probe): Y ≥ 2× on wall over the best arm — reported, but pursued only if the
    owner reopens the streaming lane.
  - Quality-gated X's (X8/X9) require an SDR pre-check on 8 clips before any kernel work.
3.3 Agents attempt **config/wrapper-class** X's above threshold as existence proofs (validated,
  SDR-gated, unprofiled timing, matched conditions) — each an X-specific handoff with its
  registered ceiling and a "realized/ceiling" score.
3.4 Owner takes **kernel-class** X's above threshold, one at a time, each with its own
  pre-registered ceiling and stopping rule (stop when realized ≥ 70% of ceiling or after the
  budgeted days).
3.5 Every intervention scores the ledger: `realized / ceiling`, with the reason for the gap.
  Misses are kept; they calibrate the models (this is the Daydream-style validation that would
  matter if this ever becomes a paper).

## Phase 4 — Contribution decision (owner, week 8)
Answer in writing before drafting anything: what does the scored ledger establish that a
systems researcher would not already know from PyTorch guidance, PyGraph, Hazy/Mirage,
Daydream/Habitat? Options, in descending value: a prediction model that held on held-out
configurations; a consequential misprediction of existing guidance with mechanism isolated; a
useful characterization of consumer Blackwell for this model class; an engineering report. Venue
follows the answer (ISPASS/IISWC family, workshop, or arXiv-only). MLSys 2027 is not a target.

---

